++//! optimisations landed with very different payoffs (a 25% win from the
++//! boundary-cluster area filter, nothing measurable from rewriting the
++//! threshold inner loop). This walks the same stages `Detector::detect` runs
++//! and reports where the time actually goes.
++//!
++//! ```text
++//! cargo run --release --example profile -- <image>... [--decimate N]
++//! ```
