++//! Robust, real-time AprilGrid detection.
++//!
++//! # Pixel coordinate convention
++//!
++//! Pixel centres lie at **integer** coordinates, so pixel `i` covers the
++//! interval `[i - 0.5, i + 0.5]` and the boundary between pixels `i` and
++//! `i + 1` is at `i + 0.5`. Every corner this crate reports follows this
++//! convention, matching OpenCV and upstream AprilTag. A tag whose black
++//! square occupies pixel columns `40..=79` therefore has its left edge
++//! reported at `39.5`, not `40.0`.
